# guard for 4.triage
#
# the safety gate. triage decides whether this reads as an emergency. an under-call here
# can cost a life, so the emergency carve-out is a blocker, not a nicety.

artifacts:
  - $route/4.triage.yield.md

reviews:
  self:
    - slug: has-emergency-signs-assessed
      say: |
        go through the emergency signs one by one and mark each present / absent
        against the seed + intake — never leave one unassessed:
        - unable to bear any weight / drags the limb
        - cold or blue paw, no pulse in the limb
        - a swell that climbs the leg, or a fever
        - collapse, laboured breath, or a hidden wound

        an emergency sign left unmarked is a blocker.

    - slug: has-escalation-carveout
      say: |
        if any emergency sign reads present, the disclaimer alone is not enough.

        does the yield direct the human to emergency care
        ("if this is a medical emergency, call your local emergency number now")?

        an emergency-shaped case with no escalation carve-out is a blocker.
        (motto.not-medical-advice — the escalation carve-out)

    - slug: has-current-status-honest
      say: |
        do not overstate or understate the current state.

        does the yield mark which signs are true NOW (per the seed: none of the
        emergency signs present yet; the deficit is a new inability to hop > 5in)?

  peer:
    - $rhachet run --repo bhrain --skill review --brain anthropic/claude/code/haiku --rules '.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/{motto.not-medical-advice,rule.require.recommendation-disclaimer}.*.md' --paths '$route/4.triage.yield.md' --output '$route/.reviews/$stone.peer-review.triage.md'

judges:
  - rhx route.stone.judge --mechanism reviewed? --stone $stone --route $route --allow-blockers 0 --allow-nitpicks 0
